h3. {color:#36b37e}Compensations{color}

* We have 20 processes/articles for the situations which will be solved with AI. 
* {color:#006644}*In 10 processes actions fully match the AI rules*{color}, or if not fully, then the difference does not disrupt their coexistence.
** _E.g. 1 “Driver refused destination”_ - our process offers a small sum comp only if R is upset. AI offers a small sum comp only if R is pushing for it. 
** _E.g. 2 “Driver was impolite”_ - our process doesn’t offer any comp. AI offers a small sum comp if R is pushing for it.
* {color:#bf2600}*In 10 processes actions do not match with the AI rules*{color}{color:#bf2600}.{color}
** _E.g. 1 “Overcharges”_ - in our processes the compensation actions are related to overcharge reasons, while AI doesn’t consider the reasons, but the % of the overcharge. 
** _E.g. 2 “I was charged cash for in-app” -_ our process action gives a full refund if the rider actually paid twice, while AI doesn’t provide full compensation, only a small sum if R is pushing for it. {color:#bf2600}_I need to understand how the AI will work if R’s contact reason is “Driver behavior” but there is an overcharge too, will AI apply the rule only by the contact reason, or it will be able to switch?_{color}
