{quote}“Are the number of chats per order increasing/decreasing over time?”{quote}

[~accountid:6203dde78df9a200718e788a] If a chat feature is enabled almost always there will be a chat created for the order. This doesn’t depend on the user behaviour (at least it’s not a behaviour towards chats). As soon as order is placed the Rider app requests available contact options and this triggers creating a chat. This happens only if the active order screen is on top, which almost always is, unless the user places an order and turns off the screen until the driver comes and changes the order status to {{Driving to Destination}} (in this case there is chance the available contact options won't be called until user taps the Driver profile icon).

Besides there can’t be more than 1 chat per order, so does this trend still make sense to you? Maybe we should have a different trend, like {{Active chats per Order}} where chat is considered as Active if there is at least one message there. Does it make sense?

